 The `data` field is always encoded as JSON. You can pass any value that can be serialized as JSON, including Pydantic models.
 
+/// note
+
+The `event` and `id` fields must be single-line values: they can't contain line breaks (`\r` or `\n`), and `id` can't contain null characters (`\0`). Those characters would break the event stream, so FastAPI raises an error instead of sending invalid data.
+
+///
+
 ## Raw Data { #raw-data }
 
 If you need to send data **without** JSON encoding, use `raw_data` instead of `data`.
